## Approach

Three pieces: (1) SPEED3 numerical differentiation mode, requiring a refactor to separate the inner dispatch from the public `calc` entry point; (2) `calc_ut` convenience method; (3) proper ECL_NUT output extraction and expanded integration golden tests. The SPEED3 refactor is the bulk — it needs the inner body dispatch to return the raw 24-element array so the 3-call central-difference can operate on it before final extraction. The /32 review fix for ECL_NUT RADIANS (strip RADIANS entirely) was a stopgap — the C ref doc shows RADIANS should convert all 4 ECL_NUT values, which this task will implement properly.

