### Step 2: Fix ECL_NUT output extraction

The /32 review fix strips RADIANS for ECL_NUT to prevent mixed-unit output. The C ref doc (§2, line 163) shows the correct behavior: for ECL_NUT, RADIANS converts all 4 values `[0..3]` (not the normal 2-slot conversion). Replace the current ECL_NUT branch in `context.rs`:

```rust
if body == Body::EclipticNutation {
    let ecl_nut = crate::calc::calc_ecl_nut(jd_tt, flags, models);
    return Ok(CalcResult {
        data: crate::calc::extract_ecl_nut(&ecl_nut, flags),
        flags_used: flags,
    });
}
```

Add `extract_ecl_nut` in `calc.rs`. This is a separate function because ECL_NUT has fundamentally different output semantics: 4 angular values in a flat array (no 24-element save area, no EQUATORIAL/XYZ meaning):

```rust
pub fn extract_ecl_nut(ecl_nut: &[f64; 6], flags: CalcFlags) -> [f64; 6] {
    // C behavior: EQUATORIAL/XYZ produce zeros (data only lives in slots 0-5
    // of the save area; offsets 6+/12+ are empty). Copy 4 values, not 3+speed.
    if flags.intersects(CalcFlags::EQUATORIAL | CalcFlags::XYZ) {
        return [0.0; 6];
    }
    let mut data = *ecl_nut;
    if flags.contains(CalcFlags::RADIANS) {
        // C ref doc §2 line 163: ECL_NUT RADIANS converts [0..3]
        for v in &mut data[..4] {
            *v *= DEGTORAD;
        }
    }
    data
}
```

### Step 3: Refactor calc into inner dispatch + SPEED3 wrapper

The current `Ephemeris::calc` does flag normalization, body dispatch, and output extraction in one method. SPEED3 needs to call the inner dispatch 3 times at different JDs, so split into:

**Inner dispatch** (`calc_inner` on Ephemeris, private) — takes normalized flags, returns `Result<[f64; 24], Error>` for planet-like bodies. ECL_NUT and Earth are handled before this is called.

```rust
fn calc_inner(&self, jd_tt: f64, body: Body, flags: CalcFlags) -> Result<[f64; 24], Error> {
    let models = &self.config.astro_models;
    if matches!(body, Body::MeanNode | Body::MeanApogee) {
        if flags.intersects(CalcFlags::HELCTR | CalcFlags::BARYCTR) {
            return Ok([0.0; 24]);
        }
        return match body {
            Body::MeanNode => crate::calc::calc_mean_node(jd_tt, flags, models),
            Body::MeanApogee => crate::calc::calc_mean_apogee(jd_tt, flags, models),
            _ => unreachable!(),
        };
    }
    if flags.intersects(CalcFlags::HELCTR | CalcFlags::BARYCTR) {
        return Err(Error::UnsupportedFlags(
            flags & (CalcFlags::HELCTR | CalcFlags::BARYCTR),
        ));
    }
    let eps_j2000 = crate::obliquity::obliquity(J2000, CalcFlags::empty(), models);
    match body {
        Body::Sun => crate::calc::calc_sun(jd_tt, &eps_j2000, flags, models),
        Body::Moon => crate::calc::calc_moon(jd_tt, &eps_j2000, flags, models),
        Body::Mercury | ... | Body::Pluto => {
            crate::calc::calc_planet(jd_tt, body, &eps_j2000, flags, models)
        }
        _ => Err(Error::EphemerisNotAvailable { body, source: EphemerisSource::Moshier }),
    }
}
```

**Public calc** — handles ECL_NUT/Earth early returns, then either SPEED3 path or direct path:

```rust
pub fn calc(&self, jd_tt: f64, body: Body, flags: CalcFlags) -> Result<CalcResult, Error> {
    let flags = crate::calc::plaus_iflag(flags);
    // ... unsupported flags check ...
    // ... ECL_NUT early return ...
    // ... Earth early return ...

    if flags.contains(CalcFlags::SPEED3) {
        return self.calc_speed3(jd_tt, body, flags);
    }

    let xreturn = self.calc_inner(jd_tt, body, flags)?;
    Ok(CalcResult {
        data: crate::calc::extract_output(&xreturn, flags),
        flags_used: flags,
    })
}
```

### Step 4: Implement SPEED3

`src/context.rs` — private method on Ephemeris:

```rust
fn calc_speed3(&self, jd_tt: f64, body: Body, flags: CalcFlags) -> Result<CalcResult, Error> {
    let dt = crate::calc::speed3_interval(body);
    // Inner calls use SPEED (not SPEED3) so they compute position + analytical speed
    let inner_flags = (flags & !CalcFlags::SPEED3) | CalcFlags::SPEED;

    let x0 = self.calc_inner(jd_tt - dt, body, inner_flags)?;
    let x2 = self.calc_inner(jd_tt + dt, body, inner_flags)?;
    let mut x1 = self.calc_inner(jd_tt, body, inner_flags)?;

    crate::calc::denormalize_positions(&mut x0, &x1, &mut x2);
    crate::calc::calc_speed_3point(&mut x1, &x0, &x2, dt);

    Ok(CalcResult {
        data: crate::calc::extract_output(&x1, flags | CalcFlags::SPEED),
        flags_used: flags,
    })
}
```

`src/calc.rs` — three helper functions:

```rust
pub fn speed3_interval(body: Body) -> f64 {
    match body {
        Body::Moon => MOON_SPEED_INTV,     // 0.00005
        Body::OscuApogee | Body::TrueNode => 0.1,  // NODE_CALC_INTV_MOSH
        _ => PLAN_SPEED_INTV,              // 0.0001
    }
}

pub fn denormalize_positions(x0: &mut [f64; 24], x1: &[f64; 24], x2: &mut [f64; 24]) {
    // Unwrap ±180° discontinuities in degree-valued angular slots.
    // Position slots only (0-2, 6-8, 12-14, 18-20). Harmless for
    // non-angular values since they never exceed ±180.
    for i in [0, 1, 2, 6, 7, 8, 12, 13, 14, 18, 19, 20] {
        if x0[i] - x1[i] < -180.0 { x0[i] += 360.0; }
        if x0[i] - x1[i] > 180.0 { x0[i] -= 360.0; }
        if x2[i] - x1[i] < -180.0 { x2[i] += 360.0; }
        if x2[i] - x1[i] > 180.0 { x2[i] -= 360.0; }
    }
}

pub fn calc_speed_3point(x1: &mut [f64; 24], x0: &[f64; 24], x2: &[f64; 24], dt: f64) {
    // Central difference: speed = (x2 - x0) / (2 * dt)
    // Overwrite speed slots (3-5, 9-11, 15-17, 21-23) in the center result
    let dt2 = 2.0 * dt;
    for base in [0, 6, 12, 18] {
        for j in 0..3 {
            x1[base + 3 + j] = (x2[base + j] - x0[base + j]) / dt2;
        }
    }
}
```

