## Key architectural notes

1. **ECL_NUT extraction** (from c-ref-calc.md §2 line 163): C copies 4 elements and converts all 4 with RADIANS. EQUATORIAL/XYZ produce zeros because the 24-element save area is never populated for ECL_NUT. `extract_ecl_nut` encodes this directly rather than routing through the generic `extract_output`.

2. **SPEED3 vs SPEED**: C `swe_calc` handles SPEED3 as a wrapper around `swecalc`. Our equivalent: `calc` wraps `calc_inner`. The inner dispatch always uses SPEED (analytical speed). SPEED3 replaces those speeds with central-difference speeds post-hoc.

3. **denormalize_positions**: Applies ±180° unwrap to all position slots. Cartesian and distance values are in AU (0-50 range) and never trigger the threshold, so applying uniformly is safe and avoids slot-specific logic.

4. **Default SPEED**: C adds SPEED when neither SPEED nor SPEED3 is set. Our existing golden tests pass because the C generator explicitly includes SPEED in "default" flags (0x104 = MOSEPH|SPEED). Adding this to plaus_iflag matches C and prevents silent speed omission for callers who forget the flag.
